* SCRIP keeps label-scanning text physically AFTER a valid END statement; SPITBOL stops at END.
* Two identical trailing lines here trigger a spurious "duplicate label" parse error in scrip.
* Root cause behind csnobol4_suite/sudoku.sno, where the puzzle-grid text after END repeats a
* row verbatim.  sbl -bf prints "hi" cleanly (rc=0); scrip refuses to compile at all.
	OUTPUT = 'hi'
END
